Xviewer source package notes
============================

Upstream selection
------------------

The current Xviewer release is version 3.4.16 under the release tag
master.lmde7. At the time this packaging was prepared, that release tag and
the upstream master branch both pointed to the same commit. Use the release
source archive when preparing the package:

    upstream_version=3.4.16
    upstream_tag=master.lmde7
    wget -O ../xviewer-${upstream_version}.tar.gz \
      https://github.com/linuxmint/xviewer/archive/refs/tags/${upstream_tag}.tar.gz
    mk-origtargz --package xviewer --version ${upstream_version}+ds \
      --repack --compression xz ../xviewer-${upstream_version}.tar.gz
    gbp import-orig --pristine-tar --upstream-version=${upstream_version}+ds \
      ../xviewer_${upstream_version}+ds.orig.tar.xz

Do not use the release's packages.tar.gz or pre-built .deb files as the source
input. They are Linux Mint binary artifacts, whereas Debian must build from
source.

The release tag may change in the future. That is not a problem for a later
package update: inspect the new release's Meson version, change
debian/changelog to the new Debian version, and import its archive. Once
imported, the orig tarball and pristine-tar metadata preserve the exact source
used for this Debian version.

Repacking
---------

Files-Excluded in debian/copyright removes the upstream debian directory from
the orig tarball. That directory is Linux Mint packaging and must not be mixed
with this Debian packaging. Do not remove the rest of the Linux Mint Xviewer
source: it is the upstream project and its copyright and license notices must
be retained. The +ds suffix records this repacking.

Clean validation before sponsorship
-----------------------------------

A Debian 13 build is useful for local development. Before requesting
sponsorship, rebuild the source package in a clean Debian unstable environment:

    dpkg-buildpackage --build=source --no-sign
    sbuild -d unstable ../xviewer_3.4.16+ds-1.dsc

Inspect every Lintian finding:

    lintian --display-info --display-experimental --pedantic \
      ../xviewer_3.4.16+ds-1_*.changes

Run the installed-package tests:

    autopkgtest ../xviewer_3.4.16+ds-1_amd64.changes \
      -- schroot unstable-amd64-sbuild

Also install the generated xviewer package in a fresh graphical Debian virtual
machine and manually test image opening, navigation, zoom, rotation, save,
print preview, fullscreen, slideshow, metadata, plugins, and help.

Salsa continuous integration
----------------------------

The root .gitlab-ci.yml starts Salsa CI automatically when the repository is
imported as a Salsa project. Debian's preferred long-term setup is to select
debian/salsa-ci.yml as the project's CI/CD configuration file in Salsa. Both
files include the same official Debian recipe; keep only the active entry if a
sponsor or packaging team requests that the duplicate be removed.

Before requesting sponsorship
-----------------------------

Keep the changelog distribution as UNRELEASED while developing. After clean
builds and tests, use dch --release --distribution unstable to finalize it.
Build and sign the source package with debuild -S -sa, upload the resulting
source changes file to mentors.debian.net, and file a Request for Sponsorship.

Bug #830615 is the existing Request for Package for Xviewer. Retitle it to an
Intent To Package and set yourself as its owner before requesting sponsorship.
The changelog's Closes entry will close it only after the package is accepted
into the Debian archive.
